    "body": "`Position()` is `(-1, -1)` before the first flush, so `down := h - y - 1` comes out as `h`, not 0. A one-line view still emits `ESC[1B` and leaves a blank row above the printed line. `if y < 0 { y = 0 }` inside the same guard fixes it.",
